sd: under LOK a font name sets Western text, and CJK when it can

Impress applied a chosen font name to the script at the cursor or in
the selection when editing text, and to Western text only when a
shape was selected; the state at a bare cursor followed the input
language, which under LOK is the worker host's keyboard. In ElyShow a
font picked at the end of Latin text set only the Western font, and
Chinese typed after kept the slide's default Asian font: picking
Microsoft YaHei left the Chinese characters in another face (Ely
GitHub #83). Under LOK Impress now does what Writer does since patch
0055: the name always sets the Western font, and the CJK font too
when the font is installed and has CJK glyphs, both while editing and
with the shape selected; the font state at a bare cursor follows the
script there.

